sequenceDiagram
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant GH as GitHub Actions runner<br/>(x86_64, ubuntu-latest)
    participant DH as Docker Hub
    participant Neon as Neon Postgres<br/>(direct, non-pooled endpoint)

    box Netcup VPS -- x86_64, Vienna
    participant Comp as Docker Compose CLI<br/>(project: kanban-board-backend)
    participant App as app
    participant Caddy as caddy
    participant RP as redpanda
    end

    Dev->>GH: push to master (the workflow's only trigger)

    GH->>GH: setup -- derive base_image_name from<br/>DOCKERHUB_USER/DOCKERHUB_REPOSITORY

    GH->>GH: run-tests (needs: setup)<br/>./gradlew test, then ./gradlew spotlessCheck<br/>Temurin JDK 21
    Note over GH: run-tests gates every job below --<br/>nothing downstream runs unless this succeeds

    par build-and-push-docker-image (needs: [setup, run-tests])
        GH->>GH: derive IMAGE_TAG from commit short SHA<br/>(${GITHUB_SHA::7})
        GH->>DH: build linux/amd64 natively (no QEMU --<br/>runner and VM share x86_64) and push image
    and flyway-verify (needs: [setup, run-tests])
        GH->>GH: refuse if configured DB host carries<br/>Neon's pooled ("-pooler") marker
        GH->>Neon: Flyway CLI container `migrate`<br/>against direct endpoint, sslmode=require
        Note over GH,Neon: applies this commit's migrations to the REAL<br/>production database now -- before the new image<br/>ever reaches the VM. Schema change and the code<br/>that consumes it are not deployed atomically.
    end

    GH->>Comp: deploy-to-netcup (needs: [build-and-push-docker-image, flyway-verify])<br/>scp docker-compose.prod.yml, Caddyfile over SSH<br/>(host key pinned by fingerprint)
    Note right of Comp: no --remove-orphans/rm -- the VM's<br/>never-committed .env.prod survives untouched
    Note over GH,Comp: concurrency group "deploy-to-netcup-vm":<br/>a second push mid-deploy QUEUES rather than cancels,<br/>so this scp step is never interrupted half-copied
    GH->>Comp: export IMAGE_TAG (commit short SHA) into the SSH shell<br/>(a shell var outranks --env-file precedence,<br/>so this commit's freshly built tag always wins)
    GH->>Comp: docker compose pull app
    Comp->>DH: pull app image<br/>(the VM pulls, not the runner)

    GH->>Comp: docker compose up -d
    Note over Comp: top-level `name: kanban-board-backend` pins project<br/>identity, and every named volume's project-prefixed name,<br/>independent of the working directory this runs from --<br/>Compose resolves to the ALREADY-RUNNING stack<br/>instead of starting a second, unrelated one
    Comp->>Comp: diff each service's resolved config<br/>against what is currently running
    Comp->>App: recreate (image reference resolves to a new<br/>tag every deploy), started only once redpanda's<br/>service_healthy condition is met (already true,<br/>redpanda untouched)
    Comp--xCaddy: left running -- resolved config is<br/>byte-identical to what's already up (no-op, not a restart)
    Comp--xRP: left running -- resolved config is<br/>byte-identical to what's already up (no-op, not a restart)
    Note over Caddy,RP: preserves caddy's Let's Encrypt certificate<br/>(no rate-limited re-request) and redpanda's Kafka log<br/>and registered Avro subjects
    Note over Comp,RP: exactly the outcome the project-name pin buys --<br/>the fixed state of the incident in docs/INFRA_RUNBOOK.md,<br/>where a directory-derived project name produced a<br/>fresh, empty volume namespace
    Note over GH,App: honest limit: `up -d` returns once app is STARTED,<br/>not once its healthcheck passes -- nothing in this<br/>pipeline waits on that healthcheck, so a green deploy<br/>job is not by itself proof the new container reached UP

    alt run succeeded
        GH->>DH: cleanup-old-images -- attempts to delete every<br/>tag except the one just deployed
        Note over GH,DH: currently does NOT achieve that -- its DELETE<br/>calls are rejected "unauthorized" (Hub API v2 needs a<br/>token exchange, not Basic auth -- see todo<br/>2026-08-16-cleanup-old-images-delete-calls-rejected-unauthorized.md).<br/>Job reports success while tags still accumulate.
    else run failed
        GH->>DH: cleanup-unused-image -- resolves the just-pushed<br/>manifest's digest and deletes that image by digest
    end
